N5008 [temp.pre]/1: a requires-clause `requires Integral<T>` followed
directly by the declaration's type name (`T identity(T a)`).  Was KNOWNBUG
since round 152 ("function must have return type"): the restricted
constraint parser rejected an identifier followed by another identifier as
the token after the clause -- a guard needed only for the general
expression path.  Fixed 2026-09-23.
